    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge, boasting an elite 85.19 score against Mitch Keller. The combination of his leadoff positioning and a +16% boost from Keller's favorable xERA makes **Corbin Carroll** our primary engine for both counting stats and stolen bases. Similarly, **James Wood** is a priority start at 76.28; despite facing a legendary name in Max Scherzer, the matchup against his current projection profile\u2014coupled with elite xwOBA metrics\u2014gives **James Wood** significant upside. **Jose Caballero** remains a high-leverage inclusion at 73.67; while his batting order is suboptimal, his ability to exploit platoon advantages against Noah Schultz is a key strategic pivot to secure our scarce stolen base category.\n\nOur infield production is anchored by **Brice Turang** (67.97) and **Isaac Paredes** (67.28). **Brice Turang** benefits from a strong wind forecast and a prime #2 slot, which helps mitigate the efficiency drain caused by the opposing catcher's pop time. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** is projected for a productive outing against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, with his dynamic platoon advantage providing the necessary lift to clear the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold. We have opted to bench **Zach McKinstry** (48.52), who was the final cut from our starting nine; while his park factors were favorable, the combination of a daunting matchup against Kyle Bradish and a 33% rain risk made him a secondary option compared to the reliable plate appearances expected from **Edwin Arroyo** or **Austin Riley**. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Jose Caballero**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Isaac Paredes** closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" designations introduce variance across the board. While **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL, the depth provided by our bench prevents us from overextending on high-risk, low-efficiency candidates. We continue to hold **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Henry Bolte** in reserve, ready to adjust should any late-scratch announcements compromise our projected efficiency scores.",
